-- N1 example sentences, batch 4: emphasis, concession, and listing.
--
-- 〜もさることながら, 〜にして, 〜と思いきや, 〜にあらず, 〜ばこそ, 〜であれ,
-- 〜なり〜なり, 〜だの〜だの, 〜つ〜つ and 〜ことなく.
--
-- THREE TOPICS SKIPPED, and the reason is the same each time — the pattern
-- itself ends in a particle, or is bare kana the index does not hold:
--
--   〜ところを (tokoro-wo): the glossary loads grammar PATTERNS as entries, so
--   ところを is matched whole and glossed correctly — and `check:examples`
--   then reports "particle swallowed", because its rule is that a multi-
--   character token ending in を with a gloss is a mistake. Here it is not,
--   but every sentence the topic can have trips it, so none can be validated.
--
--   〜うが〜まいが (you-ga-you-ga): same trap on まいが, and worse — 食べまいが
--   was matched as a form of 食べる and glossed "to eat".
--
--   〜まい (mai): まい alone shreds to ま|い in every position tried —
--   来るまい, 降るまい, 言うまい, あるまい, 行くまいと.
--
-- 〜だの〜だの, 〜つ〜つ and 〜ことなく were brought forward from 441-443 in
-- their place. Note that 〜つ〜つ survives only as its set phrases —
-- 行きつ戻りつ and 持ちつ持たれつ — which is all the pattern really has.
--
-- Two rewordings: 難しかった shredded to 難|しか|っ|た (the same past-tense
-- gap batch 3 hit on 楽しかった), and この shreds to こ|の.
--
-- Additive, idempotent, safe on a live database.

